<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moscow</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moscow is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, which grew from a minor principality into the centre of the Russian state. Polish-Lithuanian forces occupied Moscow during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles">Time of Troubles</a> in the early seventeenth century. Although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> moved the capital to St Petersburg, Moscow remained the economic and spiritual heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="Moscow" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Department of State · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Basil%27s_Cathedral_and_the_Red_Square.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
